      timeline: [
        'Pre-20th century: Game believed to be of European origin.',
        '20th century: Documented in English-language domino rulebooks.',
        'Present: Played as a family and recreational domino game worldwide.',
      ],
      evolution: "Bergen's distinctive 'matching-ends' scoring system — awarding points for double headers and triple headers — sets it apart from pip-count scoring games like Muggins. The ability to play with larger domino sets (double-9, double-12) for more players was a later adaptation.",
      cultural: 'Bergen is a straightforward domino game favoured for teaching domino fundamentals to new players due to its simple scoring principle.',
    },
    setupContent: {
