        },
        prompts: {
          human: "The open ends of the line are [3] and [3] — a double header worth 2 points to whoever created it. Your tiles: [3|5], [3|1], [6|6]. Playing [3|5] extends the left end from [3] to [5], breaking the double header. Playing [3|1] extends to [1], also breaking it. Consider holding [6|6] — it can't play here, but doubles are valuable for future triple headers.",
          ai: 'Game: Bergen. 28 dominoes (double-6). 2–4 players. Extend a single line from both ends by matching pip values. Score when both open ends match: 2pts double header, 3pts triple header (one end is a double tile). Going out = 2pts. First to 15pts (2p) or 10pts (3–4p) wins.',
        },
        scoring: {
          description: 'Double header (both ends match) = 2 pts. Triple header (both ends match, one is a double tile) = 3 pts. Going domino = 2 pts. Blocked game = 2 pts to lightest hand.',
